@node Standard Library
@chapter Standard Library

@cindex standard library
@cindex stdlib
@command{cgra init} installs a small standard library of modes and pipelines
into @file{~/.config/cgra/stdlib/}.  Pull pieces into your own configuration
with @code{include "@var{name}.cgra"}, or load a file in place with
@env{CGRA_PATH}.  Immediates marked ``@code{--imm}'' are overridden per run.

@table @file
@item arithmetic.cgra
@code{neg} (@code{-a}), @code{inc}, @code{dec}, @code{double}, @code{square}
(@code{a*a}), @code{absval}, @code{maxi}/@code{mini} (against
@code{--imm}); pipeline @code{clamp_0_100}.
@item linalg.cgra
@code{scale} (@code{a*imm}), @code{bias} (@code{a+imm}),
@code{axpy_step} (@code{a+b}); pipeline @code{affine} (@code{2*a+1}).
Full matrix work is done by the dedicated commands @command{cgra matvec},
@command{cgra conv} and @command{cgra run dot}, which take matrix-shaped input.
@item dsp.cgra
@code{gain} (@code{a*imm}), @code{attenuate} (@code{a >> imm}),
@code{rectify} (@code{max(a,0)}), @code{bias_dsp} (DC offset),
@code{accumulate} (running sum).
@item crypto.cgra
@code{xor_key}, @code{and_mask}, @code{or_bits}, @code{shl_key}, @code{add_key}
(all keyed by @code{--imm}); pipeline @code{feistel_toy}
(@code{(a ^ 42) + 7}, illustrative only---not secure).
@end table

@noindent
Example, using @code{square} directly from the in-tree library:

@example
CGRA_PATH=sw/config/stdlib cgra run square -d sim --a "2 3 4 5"
    @result{} 4 9 16 25
@end example
